WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
Panama declares a state of emergency after two major earthquakes damage buildings across every province. This is Omni View, episode 202. The government issued the declaration on Saturday after Friday's shaking, which the United States Geological Survey measured at 7.7 and 6.6. Officials reported 27 injuries and no deaths. More than 100 after shocks were recorded, some reaching magnitude 5.8. The first quake struck at a depth of 10 kilometers, about 10 kilometers

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.140
southwest of the remote community of Petalosa-Arriba in Herrera Province.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.680
The second followed shortly afterward.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.360
The shaking toppled buildings near the epicenter and prompted evacuations, with damage also

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.960
reported in neighboring Colombia.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.260
The Guardian describes damage concentrated in central provinces, including Viragua, Herrera,

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.680
Coclei, and Los Santos, where landslides cut off some communities and left residents waiting

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.240
outdoors for official guidance.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:03.040
The local resident Tony Jimenez, whose home partially collapsed in La Vila de Los Santos,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.700
told the paper the shaking was the most intense he had experienced in 90 years.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.960
Presidential Minister Juan Carlos Oriolac announced the emergency during a news conference

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.940
in Panama City, citing harm to homes, schools, healthcare facilities, roads, and hotels.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:24.940
The National Civil Protection System reported that 420 homes and an equal number of public schools

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:30.820
had been damaged, along with seven hotels at least 13 churches and nine bridges. Two

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.700
indigenous territories were affected as well. Officials will continue damage assessments and

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.960
issue guidance to residents still waiting in streets or temporary shelters. New Ebola cases

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.740
have appeared in Eastern Democratic Republic of Congo or DRC, while Kenya confirmed a fatal

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:52.060
imported infection. Health authorities are tracing contacts in both countries to limit further

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:57.760
transmission, Al Jazeera reports. The imported case in Kenya and the ongoing cases in the

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:03.540
DRC show how hard the virus is to contain once it crosses a border. Contact tracing teams

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.780
are now operating in affected Eastern DRC zones and at Kenyan entry points to identify

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:15.480
any additional exposures. The World Health Organization, or WHO, has noted the absence of confirmed

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.140
ongoing transmission chains so far, though diagnostic uncertainty remains.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.580
remains. Laboratory verification of suspected cases continues while border surveillance protocols

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:31.520
remain active. Russia has formed a battalion of Ukrainian prisoners of war and former servicemen

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:37.420
to fight against Ukrainian forces. The unit, named the Maxim Krivonis battalion, contains

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.660
several dozen fighters according to available footage. Deutscheweller reports, accounts

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:49.220
of such units began emerging in late 2022, and in August 2026 several detachments were merged

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.660
into the so-called Ukrainian Volunteer Special Forces Brigade.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.420
An investigative team from the Ukrainian public broadcaster Suspilne has identified more

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.960
than 30 members, all former Ukrainian servicemen captured between 2023 and 2024.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.340
Everything turns on why those men are in the unit, and on how large it actually is.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.220
Former Ukrainian Lieutenant Pavlo Oliinik told Deutschewella he joined after torture and captivity,

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:19.040
security, and hope to reach the front so he could escape back to Ukrainian lines.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.380
Contacted through his lawyer, Olyonik described being electrocuted, beaten, and psychologically

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.440
tortured before accepting the offer.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:32.620
Ukrainian intelligence and analyst Pavel Luzin view the battalion as an attempt to copy Russian

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:37.560
volunteer formations that fight for Ukraine, and to push back on stories about those groups.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.320
Russian media reports claim about 200 fighters, a figure the available footage does not match.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.420
Ucranian authorities will continue monitoring the battalions' activities and the circumstances

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.340
of its members.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:56.320
Aki Abe, wife of the late Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, met Rostria Swayam Svaksong

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.740
or RSS, General Secretary Datatrea Hosebali in New Delhi.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.540
The discussion focused on strengthening India-Japan ties through cultural and people-to-people initiatives.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:07.920
The Hindu reports.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.120
reports. The hour-long meeting also included Nippon Kaigi Chairman Tomohiko Taniguchi,

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:19.240
and explored civilizational and cultural cooperation. An RSS statement emphasized a shared

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.820
interest in deepening bilateral engagement beyond government channels.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.740
Sunil Ambikar, the RSS publicity in charge, said the participants reflected that shared

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.980
interest in closer engagement between the two countries. The RSS said those involved would

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:38.580
explore avenues for collaboration to strengthen cultural ties between India and Japan.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.720
Founders of artificial intelligence or AI companies in Silicon Valley welcomed statements

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.520
from President Trump supporting industry-led safety measures rather than new government rules.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.000
Founders see self-regulation as allowing faster innovation while addressing public concerns

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.760
about model risks, AP news notes.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.720
The approach lines up with voluntary commitment some firms have already made on testing and

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:08.320
transparency. Several Silicon Valley executives have publicly endorsed the emphasis on internal

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.560
oversight rather than external mandates. That stance matches earlier pledges on model

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:19.580
evaluation and disclosure issued by major developers. Companies will publish updated safety frameworks

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:25.300
and testing protocols in the coming weeks. Finance ministers gathering in Bangkok will focus on how

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.860
Middle East conflict and elevated global debt levels are weighing on economic stability.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:30.480
Efficiency.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:35.420
Officials expect talks on how regional tensions affect energy prices and growth forecasts,

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:36.820
Reuters reports.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:42.000
Debt sustainability for lower-income countries will also feature prominently on the agenda.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:47.780
The agenda includes sessions on fiscal resilience and the spillover effects of conflict on commodity

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.280
markets.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.120
Participants will review debt-restructuring mechanisms for heavily indebted nations.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:57.660
The meetings will produce joint statements outlining coordinated policy responses.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:03.060
A Gaza Nurses Hong Kong Award is progress worth knowing after six blocked attempts to

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.480
leave for overseas study.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:10.060
Hamota Abu Oda received the Spirit of Hong Kong Award, the South China Morning Post reports.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:16.360
He completed a doctorate at Hong Kong Polytechnic University in 2021 on a fellowship, and now

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:17.000
teaches there.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.100
He had obtained a nursing degree in Gaza, but kept working, teaching, and conducting research

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:25.580
despite repeated scholarship losses caused by border restrictions.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.520
On the 7th attempt, he reached Hong Kong and finished the doctorate.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.640
He has said that giving up after the lost opportunities would have prevented him from

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.000
teaching in Hong Kong today.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:40.520
The award recognizes that academic persistence and his contributions to nursing scholarship.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:46.080
He will continue his academic work while mentoring other scholars facing similar mobility challenges.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:51.260
To really understand a disaster-time state of emergency, you have to look at the sequence

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.360
of paperwork that has to exist before extra legal powers can be switched on.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.620
A lot of coverage treats the declaration as an automatic step once the ground stops moving.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:05.500
In practice, governments first have to compile rapid damage assessments from several

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:10.800
ministries at once. Those assessments have to show that ordinary local resources are already

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:16.160
overwhelmed. Only then can the cabinet invoke the legal powers that come with the emergency label.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.120
that order is the mechanism, not a formality. It is how a listener can judge whether a declaration

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:27.420
matches the documented scope of destruction, instead of assuming every quake produces one.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:32.520
Later public counts of damaged buildings and injuries become the concrete test of whether

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:38.400
those powers were justified. The process also requires verification that aftershocks are still a

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:44.380
live risk, not only that the first shock was large. Primary documents such as seismological

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:48.560
readings and civil protection tallies are the clearest baseline for that test.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.120
Official statements still need to be read beside independent reporting from more than

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.200
one region before anyone settles on the scale of the event.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.820
The useful check is the next civil protection update, whether the damaged tallies are revised

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.780
and whether the government asks for international assistance.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.720
The Guardian frames the same destruction through people cut off by landslides and waiting

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:15.080
outdoors for guidance. Panama's authorities frame it as an inventory of homes, schools,

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:21.040
hotels, churches, and bridges. Looking back over the week just gone, a few threads moved while

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:26.200
you may have been elsewhere. Taiwan set a record defense budget meant to deter war with China.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:32.300
A decision that bears on security for its 23 million residents, while the island's top chipmaker

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.300
posted a 55% sales jump last month as demand for AI chips kept rising.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:42.920
Yemen's government launched a major offensive against Houthi-held territory, testing whether

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.620
outside powers can keep that fighting from spreading into key shipping lanes.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:51.220
Quebec's new separatist government pledged an independence referendum, even though

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.980
it won only a minority of seats.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:58.340
North Korea's warning to the United States over Taiwan arms deliveries pointed to a tighter

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:02.280
alignment with Russia, with knock-on risk for East Asian security.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.740
Laboratories are still verifying suspected Ebola cases linked to Eastern Congo and Kenya,

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.820
and any additional confirmed infection is the next hard public update.

